				{
					id: "1A62AF153DAD56BE"
					item: {
						Count: 1
						ForgeCaps: {
							"celestisynth:celestisynthitemstackcapabilities": {
								cs.aquaSkin: 0
							}
						}
						id: "minecraft:written_book"
						tag: {
							author: "Mr6trt"
							pages: [
								"{\"text\":\"In the ancient marble coliseums of Gorta, where the crowds howled and kings cheered, the ground ran red with glory.\\n\\nIt was there, beneath a blistering sun and a thousand roaring souls, that Xelas rose.\\nA new name. A nobody.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"But he moved like thunder and struck like prophecy.\\n\\nThe King of Gorta, enamored by blood and spectacle, saw in him not just a gladiator but a future. And so Xelas, the golden-haired titan with the storm in his eyes,\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"rose from the sand to the marble courts.\\nHe became commander. Then general. Then legend.\\nHe waged wars not with chaos, but with cold brilliance.\\nKingdom after kingdom fell not to brute force, but to a man who could see three moves ahead.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"In the boy-prince’s eyes, Xelas was more than a warrior. He was a mentor. A father. A god.\\nBut age, as it does to all men, crept in quietly.\\nHis blade slowed. His fire dimmed. And the prince now king saw opportunity.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"One banquet. One cup. One poison.\\nBut legends don’t die like common men.\\nXelas knew. And as the guards entered, he stood. The goblet fell. The king screamed. And the marble once more drank blood — this time royal.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"With trembling fingers, Xelas touched the iron circlet he wore around his neck: a twisted crown taken from the only man who ever pushed him to his edge the fallen King of Bertane, slain in a one-hour duel under crimson banners.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"“Let this,” he whispered, “be worn by the strong… and feared by the weak.”\\n\\nHe died with his eyes open.\\n\\nBut death, it seems, was only the beginning.\\n\\nThe Crown of Xelas did not fall.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"It was said to throb with memory. It bled its power into those who dared wear it. For every soul slain, it grew heavier — not in weight, but in life.\\n\\nEvery 20 enemies fallen granted a heartbeat more. A second breath. A lengthened fate.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"And when death did come… the Crown whispered.\\nRise.\\nKill ten more.\\nOr die for good. No helm, no hood, no crown of kings can coexist with it. The Crown binds itself. It feeds upon the soul.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"It cannot be removed.\\n\\nAnd the one who wears it shall wear nothing else. No armor. No shield. Only the weight of a thousand deaths and the silence of a curse too old to remember.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"They say the path to claiming it is written in fire, frost, and thunder.\\n\\nFlesh from every dragon must be tasted.\\nTheir unborn, devoured and sacrificed.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"Magic cannot be forged it must be drawn from luck itself.\\n\\nThe bearer must sip the blood of all dragonkind, with runes that tether life to death.\\n\\nTwelve times death must be cheated, willingly by totems not meant for mortals.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"And at the final hour, when strength alone is not enough, three armors shall be worn, one by one:\\nOf fire. Of curse. Of scale.\\n\\nOnly then may the Crown reveal itself… And only then will it decide if you are worthy.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"But know this.\\n\\nXelas was betrayed not by enemy steel, but by fading loyalty.\\nHis wrath sleeps in the metal.\\nAnd if it deems you false…You will never remove it.\\nYou will never rest. You will become legend...\"}"
							]
							title: "Xela's Crown"
						}
					}
					type: "item"
				}
			]
